& [Fold_6_FaultCounterargumentAndAlternative] is complete
  + [counterargument_1] SOP may be too flexible to compile
    + [answer] compilation applies only to explicit profiles and program regions; unsupported forms are preserved or rejected visibly
  + [counterargument_2] one IR may constrain useful targets
    + [answer] source meaning stays one while target profiles declare extensions, capability, and loss; incompatible meaning requires a new source or IR revision
  + [counterargument_3] neural outputs cannot be semantically exact
    + [answer] they need not be universally exact; their proposal boundary and observational proof grade are explicit
  + [counterargument_4] self-hosting creates circular trust
    + [answer] the bootstrap root and independent verifier remain outside self-certification
  + [alternative_1] separate languages per target is rejected because identity and correspondence drift become primary
  + [alternative_2] neural-first authority is rejected because provenance, hard constraints, and effects become approximate
  + [alternative_3] exact-only language is rejected because it discards the source's intended learned compilation potential
  + [alternative_4] implementation-first prototype is rejected until the purpose and compatibility contract is signed
  + [gain_delta] is medium_risk_closure

